  "term": "multiple classification",
  "definition": "Multiple classification is a way of analyzing outcomes when they are shaped by more than one grouping or context at the same time. In the example provided, student academic success was modeled while accounting for classification by both instructors and majors, rather than treating only one grouping as relevant.",
